    <time>1790101863</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>New package: comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-02 0.1.4.

This is the sixth media bundle of the ComfyUI workflow-templates set, which
openSUSE already carries as -core, -json, -media-api, -media-image,
-media-other, -media-video and -media-assets-01. The spec is the
media-assets-01 spec with the name and version changed; the only other
difference is one extra sentence in the Legal-Review-Notice recording that
this dist's own PKG-INFO declares License-Expression: MIT.

Contents: 17 webp template previews plus five provider logos. Every file was
checked by magic number rather than extension, and each image container was
parsed to confirm zero trailing bytes, so there is no executable, archive or
appended payload.

Why now, and what requires it: nothing yet. It is a prerequisite for the
pending python-comfyui-workflow-templates 0.11.68 bump, which lists
comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-02==0.1.4 as an unconditional
dependency. Both that package and this one currently sit at the older
version, so this leaf lands first and is unreferenced until the meta bump
follows.

Two things a reviewer may ask, answered up front:

templates/logo/ carries third-party provider marks (Meta, HeyGen, Fish
Audio, Pruna, sync.so) under upstream's MIT grant. Four of the five are
byte-identical to files already shipped in Factory by media-assets-01, so
this adds one new logo to an accepted precedent rather than new legal
surface.

Those same four logos are therefore duplicated across the two subpackages,
about 67 KB in total. That is upstream's own split of the asset set, and the
install prefixes differ, so there is no file conflict between them.

Built and checked locally on aarch64: rpmlint 3 packages, 0 errors, 0
warnings, 0 badness; %check imports the module under both python3.13 and
python3.14.</comment>
